    "abstract": "To intuitively analyze the impacts of climate variables on hydrological drought, we employed SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) analysis to evaluate the contribution ranking of these variables (Fig S1).According to the results obtained, potential evapotranspiration emerged as the primary climatic factor influencing hydrological processes in the study area, followed by snowmelt, temperature, and precipitation.",
    "field": "Socio-hydrology",
    "problem": "Accurately quantifying the combined, non-linear impacts of climate change and diverse human activities on runoff decline and hydrological drought intensification in semi-arid regions is a significant challenge for conventional modeling approaches.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a hybrid physics-deep learning framework to analyze and reveal the drivers of human-driven runoff decline and hydrological drought intensification in semi-arid regions over the last 40 years.",
    "task": "The task is to determine the climatic and human-driven factors causing runoff decline and hydrological drought intensification in semi-arid regions over the last 40 years using a hybrid physics-deep learning framework.",
